    ('SECTOR_XLU','UTILITIES · XLU','index','IDX_SECTOR_FUNDS',null,'the sector as the S&P 500 draws it: XLU is the line; RSPU counts every name the same; VPU (Vanguard) and IDU (iShares) are the same sector by another recipe','XLU','TR2-20261006'),
    ('SECTOR_XLB','MATERIALS · XLB','index','IDX_SECTOR_FUNDS',null,'the sector as the S&P 500 draws it: XLB is the line; RSPM counts every name the same; VAW (Vanguard) and IYM (iShares) are the same sector by another recipe','XLB','TR2-20261006'),
    ('SECTOR_XLRE','REAL ESTATE · XLRE','index','IDX_SECTOR_FUNDS',null,'the sector as the S&P 500 draws it: XLRE is the line; RSPR counts every name the same; VNQ (Vanguard) and IYR (iShares) are the same sector by another recipe','XLRE','TR2-20261006'),
    ('AEROSPACE_DEFENCE','AEROSPACE & DEFENCE','heading','INDUSTRIAL',null,'a filing shelf, not one basket: every Aerospace & Defense company we serve sits in its four cohorts (24 of 34 names); the defence fund ITA holds 19 of them. Its cohorts do not move as one (0.21 between cohorts, the same as any two industrial names), so each is read on its own.',null,'TR2-20261006'),
    ('PACKAGED_FOODS','PACKAGED FOODS','cohort','STAPLES',null,'what they sell: branded food on the shelf. FMP ''Food Confectioners'' + ''Packaged Foods''; GICS ''Packaged Foods & Meats''. Moves together -0.13 (a pair: one number, not a group test).','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('BEVERAGES','BEVERAGES','cohort','STAPLES',null,'what they sell: drinks. FMP ''Beverages - Non-Alcoholic''; GICS ''Soft Drinks & Non-alcoholic Beverages''. Alcohol (GICS ''Distillers & Vintners'', none served) would join here. Moves together 0.45 (sector 0.29).','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('HOUSEHOLD_PERSONAL','HOUSEHOLD & PERSONAL PRODUCTS','cohort','STAPLES',null,'what they sell: soap, toothpaste, tissue, over-the-counter care. FMP ''Household & Personal Products''; GICS ''Household Products'' + ''Personal Care Products''. Moves together 0.76 (sector 0.29).','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('TOBACCO','TOBACCO','cohort','STAPLES',null,'what they sell: cigarettes and nicotine. FMP ''Tobacco''; GICS ''Tobacco''. Moves together 0.57 (a pair: one number, not a group test).','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('FOOD_DISTRIBUTION','FOOD DISTRIBUTION','cohort','STAPLES',null,'what they sell: food delivered to restaurants and canteens. FMP ''Food Distribution''; GICS ''Food Distributors''. Moves together 0.50 (a pair: one number, not a group test).','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('AGRI_PRODUCTS','AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS','cohort','STAPLES',null,'what they sell: grain, oilseeds, ingredients - to food makers, not to shoppers. FMP ''Agricultural Farm Products''; GICS ''Agricultural Products & Services''. One served name: no moves-together number.','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('STAPLES_RETAIL','GROCERY & STAPLES RETAIL','cohort','STAPLES',null,'where staples are bought. FMP ''Grocery Stores'' + ''Discount Stores''; GICS ''Food Retail'' + ''Consumer Staples Merchandise Retail''. Moves together 0.42 (sector 0.29).','XLP','TR2-20261006'),
    ('FUEL_CELLS_STORAGE','FUEL CELLS & STORAGE','cohort','AI_POWERTRAIN','ENERGY_POWER','power made or stored at the data centre itself: fuel cells (BE) and long-duration batteries (EOSE). Two names today, so it is a pair, not a group test. No fund is made for it; it is read against AI POWERTRAIN.',null,'TR2-20261006'),
    ('IDX_FACTOR_GROWTH','GROWTH','cohort','IDX_FACTOR','IDX_STYLE','by rule: next-twelve-month revenue growth of 15% or more where an analyst estimate is on file (192 names); where none is on file yet, the index maker''s call stands in (VUG holds it, VTV does not). Each row says which. Fund lines: VUG against VTV.','VUG','TR2-20261006'),
    ('IDX_FACTOR_MOMENTUM','MOMENTUM','cohort','IDX_FACTOR',null,'by rule: the top fifth of the tree''s companies by six-month return (2026-04-06 to 2026-10-05; 450 names ranked). The 12-month leg is not in yet. Fund line: MTUM.','MTUM','TR2-20261006'),
    ('IDX_FACTOR_LOW_VOL','LOW VOLATILITY','cohort','IDX_FACTOR',null,'by rule: the calmest fifth by "usual day" — the middle size of a name''s daily move over six months; the market''s (SPY) is 0.48%. Not the same as "blue chip": that is closer to QUALITY (QUAL). Fund lines: SPLV, QUAL.','SPLV','TR2-20261006');
